// src/v4/extdeps/languages/python.dag
// Scope: Python 3.14 Reference primitive fact-bundles + T-11 MVP-1 grammar-data target model.
// Owns: PythonSingletonKind, PythonScalar, PythonCost, PythonIntegerPrimitiveFacts, PythonFloatPrimitiveFacts, PythonComplexPrimitiveFacts, PythonBoolPrimitiveFacts, PythonSingletonPrimitiveFacts, python_*_facts, python_*_facts_catalog, python_facts_node, python_*_primitive_bundle, python_model_core_wave1, py_bool_grounding.
// Consumes: v4.std.model_core (ModelCore + axis symbols), v4.std.collection, v4.std.node, v4.std.logic, v4.std.algebra.
// Status: T-4 python slice — Python Reference primitives (not CPython library types); int is honestly width-axis-omitted (unbounded — see C-PYINT below); ModelCore.primitives filled via fold; inhabitance/laws/effects/partiality empty (wave-2+); `python_model_core_wave1` itself is 🟡 E-6(b) consumer-less until PythonLanguageModel lands (wave-2). canonical-B bool decl-ref is 🟡 E-6(b) staging (mirrors rust slice).
// Anchor: https://docs.python.org/3.14/reference/datamodel.html
//
// C-PYINT — Python `int` carries no `width` / `signedness` / `overflow_disposition` axis.
// The reference defines `int` as an unbounded, signed integer with arbitrary precision; there
// is no overflow event. We honestly omit the axis bindings rather than fabricate a width tag
// (per fact-bundle reseed: "model the facts read from the spec, never a hollow alias").

